  "caveats": [
    "The identity is a NECESSARY condition for the pairing to be a function of the link rather than of the braid word, not a proof that the binding functional must be a link invariant. That premise is stated, not derived, and is the remaining work in qou-gba1.",
    "The sign of P never enters this test. The two weight families disagree on the sign at A=3 and A=4 (bean qou-za3q), so a criterion that used the sign would be selection against the target (AGENTS.md). Stabilisation covariance is independent of it.",
    "Positive stabilisation only. The other Markov move, conjugation beta -> alpha beta alpha^-1, needs negative crossings, which this germ machinery does not build; it is untested here."
